<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The three built-in personalities. Sources are cited per value; anything marked "unsourced" is SimWorld's
    own and is kept, not invented. persona is a SimWorld hook for the narrator's in-fiction name; the name
    itself is still open (Scribe/Historian/The Chronicle), so every storyteller currently uses the same
    placeholder.

    Values the wiki prints are RimWorld's, on pages that name no game version:
      https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Raid_points   (the starting factor and the adaptation numbers)
      https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Cassandra_Classic
      https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Phoebe_Chillax
      https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Randy_Random
  -->

  <!--
    What every storyteller shares. RimWorld's three storytellers carry one set of these curves, and the wiki
    prints one, so they live once here rather than three times.

    pointsFactorFromDaysPassed is RimWorld's "starting factor": an EARLY-GAME DISCOUNT, never a multiplier
    above 1. https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Raid_points ("Starting factor") gives 0.7 at day 10 and earlier and
    1.0 from day 40, and says nothing about the days between; the straight line between the two printed
    points is the plain reading and is the only thing here the page does not state. This replaces an
    approximation that read (0,1) (20,2) (100,4) — a growth curve that quadrupled every raid by day 100 on
    the calendar alone, which RimWorld's formula has no term for.
  -->
  <StorytellerDef Name="StorytellerBase" Abstract="True">
    <pointsFactorFromDaysPassed>
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.7)</li>
        <li>(10, 0.7)</li>
        <li>(40, 1)</li>
      </points>
    </pointsFactorFromDaysPassed>
  </StorytellerDef>

  <!--
    Cassandra Classic. https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Cassandra_Classic ("Code specifics") prints her major-threat
    cycle and her Misc comp; the page names no game version. Everything the page prints is below, with the
    port's old value where it differed:

      ThreatBig OnOffCycle   minDaysPassed 11.0 (was 6)   onDays 4.6 (was 6.8)   offDays 6.0 (was 1.5)
                             minSpacingDays 1.9 (was 1.5) numIncidentsRange 1~2 (was 1~1)
      Misc mtbDays 4.8       (was 3.0, but that was one comp pooling six categories; see below)

    The old cycle kept threats "on" 82% of the time from day 6 (6.8 of every 8.3 days). RimWorld's is on for
    4.6 of every 10.6 days, 43%, from day 11, and the page's own worked table of on-phases (11-15.6, 21.6-26.2,
    32.2-36.8, 42.8-47.4, ...) is what IncidentCycleUtility reproduces.

    Not on the page, therefore SimWorld's own and kept as they were (UNSOURCED): the ClassicIntro (the page
    says a mad animal, then a single raider on day 5 hour 15; the port sends one ManhunterPack on day 4), the
    ThreatSmall cycle (no shipped incident is in that category, so it fires nothing), the weights of the other
    categories, and the disease interval.

    Splitting the old RandomMain in two is the one structural change. The page's 4.8 is for Misc alone; the old
    comp rolled once every 3.0 days and then chose among Misc 40, FactionArrival 20 and four categories of 5,
    so Misc was effectively one event per 6 days and each other category w/240 per day. Misc now has its own
    comp at the page's 4.8. The rest keep exactly the rate they had: 40 weight units at mtbDays 6.0 gives the
    same w/240 per day each.
  -->
  <StorytellerDef ParentName="StorytellerBase">
    <defName>Cassandra_Classic</defName>
    <label>Cassandra Classic</label>
    <description>A balanced storyteller: rising tension with a fair, escalating rhythm.</description>
    <listOrder>0</listOrder>
    <persona>The Chronicle</persona>
    <comps>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: see above. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_ClassicIntro">
        <incident>ManhunterPack</incident>
        <day>4</day>
      </li>
      <!-- Sourced: the wiki's Cassandra_Classic "Major Threats" block, every field. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_OnOffCycle">
        <category>ThreatBig</category>
        <minDaysPassed>11</minDaysPassed>
        <onDays>4.6</onDays>
        <offDays>6</offDays>
        <minSpacingDays>1.9</minSpacingDays>
        <numIncidentsRange>1~2</numIncidentsRange>
      </li>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: kept. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_OnOffCycle">
        <category>ThreatSmall</category>
        <onDays>4</onDays>
        <offDays>2</offDays>
        <numIncidentsRange>1~1</numIncidentsRange>
      </li>
      <!-- Sourced: the wiki's "Misc. Events" block, mtbDays 4.8. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_RandomMain">
        <mtbDays>4.8</mtbDays>
        <maxThreatBigIntervalDays>0</maxThreatBigIntervalDays>
        <categoryWeights>
          <li><category>Misc</category><weight>1</weight></li>
        </categoryWeights>
      </li>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: the old pooled comp's other categories, at exactly the rate they had. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_RandomMain">
        <mtbDays>6.0</mtbDays>
        <maxThreatBigIntervalDays>0</maxThreatBigIntervalDays>
        <randomPointsFactorRange>0.9~1.1</randomPointsFactorRange>
        <categoryWeights>
          <li><category>FactionArrival</category><weight>20</weight></li>
          <li><category>OrbitalVisitor</category><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><category>AllyAssistance</category><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><category>GiveQuest</category><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><category>ShipChunkDrop</category><weight>5</weight></li>
        </categoryWeights>
      </li>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: kept. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_Disease">
        <category>DiseaseHuman</category>
        <baseMtbDays>10</baseMtbDays>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </StorytellerDef>

  <!--
    Phoebe Chillax. https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Phoebe_Chillax prints her cycle and a Misc comp; no game
    version named.

      ThreatBig OnOffCycle   minDaysPassed 13.0 (was 10)  onDays 8 (was 4)  offDays 8 (was 8)
                             numIncidentsRange 1~1 (was 1~1)
      Misc mtbDays 4.8       (was 5.0 for a pooled comp; same split as Cassandra's)

    The page prints no minSpacingDays, which reads as RimWorld's default of 0. The old 2 is kept (UNSOURCED);
    with one incident per sixteen-day cycle it cannot bind either way, so it moves nothing. Nor does the page
    mention an intro, the disease interval or the other categories' weights; those are kept (UNSOURCED). The
    non-Misc comp's mtbDays of 10.0 reproduces the old pooled comp's per-category rate (w/400 per day) over
    its 40 weight units.
  -->
  <StorytellerDef ParentName="StorytellerBase">
    <defName>Phoebe_Chillax</defName>
    <label>Phoebe Chillax</label>
    <description>A gentler storyteller: longer quiet stretches and a more relaxed pace.</description>
    <listOrder>1</listOrder>
    <persona>The Chronicle</persona>
    <comps>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: kept. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_ClassicIntro">
        <incident>ManhunterPack</incident>
        <day>8</day>
      </li>
      <!-- Sourced: every field the wiki prints, except minSpacingDays (UNSOURCED, kept). -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_OnOffCycle">
        <category>ThreatBig</category>
        <minDaysPassed>13</minDaysPassed>
        <onDays>8</onDays>
        <offDays>8</offDays>
        <minSpacingDays>2</minSpacingDays>
        <numIncidentsRange>1~1</numIncidentsRange>
      </li>
      <!-- Sourced: the wiki's "Misc. Events" block, mtbDays 4.8. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_RandomMain">
        <mtbDays>4.8</mtbDays>
        <maxThreatBigIntervalDays>0</maxThreatBigIntervalDays>
        <categoryWeights>
          <li><category>Misc</category><weight>1</weight></li>
        </categoryWeights>
      </li>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: the old pooled comp's other categories, at exactly the rate they had. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_RandomMain">
        <mtbDays>10.0</mtbDays>
        <maxThreatBigIntervalDays>0</maxThreatBigIntervalDays>
        <randomPointsFactorRange>0.9~1.1</randomPointsFactorRange>
        <categoryWeights>
          <li><category>FactionArrival</category><weight>20</weight></li>
          <li><category>OrbitalVisitor</category><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><category>AllyAssistance</category><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><category>GiveQuest</category><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><category>ShipChunkDrop</category><weight>5</weight></li>
        </categoryWeights>
      </li>
      <!-- UNSOURCED: kept. -->
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_Disease">
        <category>DiseaseHuman</category>
        <baseMtbDays>16</baseMtbDays>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </StorytellerDef>

  <!--
    Randy Random. https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Randy_Random prints his one comp; no game version named.

      minDaysPassed 1 (new)   mtbDays 1.35 (same)   maxThreatBigIntervalDays 13 (was 20)
      randomPointsFactorRange 0.5~1.5 (was 0.5~1.7)
      categoryWeights   Misc 3.5 (was 33)  ThreatBig 1.4 (was 16)  OrbitalVisitor 1.1 (was 5)
                        FactionArrival 2.4 (was 16)  ThreatSmall 0.6 (was 11)  ShipChunkDrop 0.22 (was 5)

    The old weights were on a scale of their own and were not proportional to these. The page's six sum to
    9.22, which puts a ThreatBig at 15.2% of his events (the page works a major threat every 7.14 days out of
    that share and the cap, reading mtbDays as a mean; Rand.MTBEventOccurs is a half-life, so the interval
    this port realises is longer, and the three kept categories below dilute the share to 12.9%).

    DiseaseHuman, AllyAssistance and GiveQuest are in his comp in the port because the port gives him no
    separate comps for them as RimWorld does; the page prints no weight for them (UNSOURCED). They keep their
    old share relative to ThreatBig (old 9, 5 and 5 against 16), re-expressed on the page's scale: x 1.4 / 16.
  -->
  <StorytellerDef ParentName="StorytellerBase">
    <defName>Randy_Random</defName>
    <label>Randy Random</label>
    <description>An unpredictable storyteller: no pattern, just chance.</description>
    <listOrder>2</listOrder>
    <persona>The Chronicle</persona>
    <comps>
      <li Class="SimWorld.Director.StorytellerCompProperties_RandomMain">
        <minDaysPassed>1</minDaysPassed>
        <mtbDays>1.35</mtbDays>
        <maxThreatBigIntervalDays>13</maxThreatBigIntervalDays>
        <randomPointsFactorRange>0.5~1.5</randomPointsFactorRange>
        <categoryWeights>
          <li><category>ThreatBig</category><weight>1.4</weight></li>
          <li><category>ThreatSmall</category><weight>0.6</weight></li>
          <li><category>Misc</category><weight>3.5</weight></li>
          <li><category>FactionArrival</category><weight>2.4</weight></li>
          <li><category>OrbitalVisitor</category><weight>1.1</weight></li>
          <li><category>ShipChunkDrop</category><weight>0.22</weight></li>
          <!-- UNSOURCED, below: kept at their old share of a ThreatBig. -->
          <li><category>DiseaseHuman</category><weight>0.79</weight></li>
          <li><category>AllyAssistance</category><weight>0.44</weight></li>
          <li><category>GiveQuest</category><weight>0.44</weight></li>
        </categoryWeights>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </StorytellerDef>

</Defs>
